# Every token below is OPTIONAL. Without one, that connector runs through Claude Code's connectors
# (snapshot every 15 min + a short claude -p per write); with one, it calls the API directly (faster).
# DATA_MODE=api|connectors forces one mode for all. CLAUDE_FETCH_MODEL picks the model for those runs.
# Copy to .env and export before running. Never commit real values.
MONDAY_API_TOKEN=
SLACK_TOKEN=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# DRY_RUN=0 enables real board/Slack writes and real Gmail drafts. Default is dry-run.
# Slack user token scopes: im:history, mpim:history, channels:history, groups:history, im:read, mpim:read, channels:read, groups:read, users:read, chat:write, im:write

# Mac only (see launchd/README.md)
# CLAUDE_BIN=/full/path/to/claude
# Command that publishes the learning log; it gets the file path in $LEARNINGLOG_FILE. Nothing is published until set.
# LEARNINGLOG_PUBLISH_CMD=
